From: cvediver <cvediver@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 12 Sep 2026 10:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: self-heal peers with a dead first TX burst

On the GL-BE9300 (IPQ5332 + 2x QCN9274, WLAN.WBE.1.6 firmware) a
station's FIRST association can come up with every downlink unicast
data frame silently lost: nothing goes out over the air, the client
never ACKs, and management/EAPOL keep working. Reassociation always
recovers, permanently. Bench reproduction shows the failure appears
only past ~3.85 days of AP uptime and only for cold first-time peer
bring-up.

Reverse engineering of the firmware images located the mechanism.
Firmware gates every peer's data TIDs at creation (TQM TID flags bit31,
"tqm tickle pending due to assoc_flag=0 peer %d", wal_tqm.c:866) and
opens them during peer_assoc through an asynchronous chain ending in
the TQM SSN-sync status callback (wal_tx_de_mgmt.c:879). That callback
returns WITHOUT tickling or clearing the pending bit if the TID is
still connection-pause module-blocked when the SSN-sync status arrives.
Nothing ever replays the tickle - re-tickle is itself gated by the
assoc flag - so the TID's downlink queue is parked in TQM forever: a
classic lost wakeup. Only a full first-time bring-up runs this chain
with the assoc-time block modules (security 0x14, BA 0x0c, MLO
0x64/0x57) still engaged; a reassociation over a warm peer skips the
SSN-sync window entirely, which is why reconnecting always fixes it.

The firmware is signature-enforced, so the fix has to live host-side,
and the wedged state is invisible to the host except through its
observable: TX attempts with zero completions right after
authorization.

Detect and heal exactly that. When an AP-mode station (including AP
MLD) transitions to AUTHORIZED, arm a one-shot wiphy delayed work 1.5 s
out and count, per station, unicast data enqueues and TQM frame-acked
completions. If the window shows >= 4 attempts and zero ACKs, log one
loud line and discard the parked frames with the existing per-station
WMI TID flush (ath12k_mac_op_flush_sta), which reaches TQM through the
flush command path and gives the client's retransmissions a fresh
enqueue; then re-check once more 1.5 s later and report whether the
flush recovered the peer. A healthy first burst disarms silently. The
check is cancelled when the station leaves AUTHORIZED or is removed,
and the counters cost nothing while the check is not armed. For MLO
stations all data rides the primary link and the flush helper already
iterates every link, so no extra MLO handling is needed. A station
with buffered-only traffic (e.g. immediately dozing) can trip a
spurious flush; the cost is one warning and a few dropped frames that
upper layers retransmit.

Also add two ath12k_info diagnostics on the ML peer ID round-robin
allocator (allocation with the cursor value, and both free sites).
The leading host-side candidate for the ~3.85 d onset is ML peer ID
recycling: the cursor never reuses an ID until max_ml_peer_ids
allocations have passed, which at the 256-ID default equals 255
association cycles, and a recycled ID re-enters firmware ML peer
state warm. One line per association makes the ID history visible on
the bench without debugfs.

Signed-off-by: cvediver <cvediver@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.h        | 11 ++++
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c         | 93 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/peer.c        |  6 +-
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/peer.h        |  2 +-
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/dp_tx.c |  8 +++
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/hw.c    |  7 +++
 6 files changed, 124 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.h b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.h
index 1a68ddf..3421f1b 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.h
@@ -539,6 +539,17 @@ struct ath12k_sta {
 	enum ieee80211_sta_state state;
 
 	bool enable_4addr;
+
+	/* First-TX-burst self-heal (firmware first-assoc lost-wakeup
+	 * workaround). The counters are only maintained while
+	 * txburst_check_armed is set, i.e. for a short window after an
+	 * AP-mode station reaches AUTHORIZED.
+	 */
+	struct wiphy_delayed_work txburst_check_wk;
+	atomic_t txburst_attempts;
+	atomic_t txburst_acked;
+	bool txburst_check_armed;
+	bool txburst_flushed;
 };
 
 #define ATH12K_HALF_20MHZ_BW	10
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
index f06f030..f791c2a 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
@@ -7401,6 +7401,9 @@ static void ath12k_mac_ml_station_remove(struct ath12k_vif *ahvif,
 		ath12k_peer_ml_quarantine(ah, ahsta, ret);
 
 	if (sta->mlo) {
+		ath12k_info(ath12k_ah_to_ar(ah, 0)->ab,
+			    "ml peer id %u freed for %pM\n",
+			    ahsta->ml_peer_id, sta->addr);
 		if (!test_bit(ahsta->ml_peer_id, ah->quarantined_ml_peer_id_map))
 			clear_bit(ahsta->ml_peer_id, ah->free_ml_peer_id_map);
 		ahsta->ml_peer_id = ATH12K_MLO_PEER_ID_INVALID;
@@ -7851,6 +7854,63 @@ static int ath12k_mac_select_links(struct ath12k_base *ab,
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/* Self-heal for AP-mode stations whose first TX burst after authorization
+ * dies silently in firmware: the TQM TID assoc gate can eat the SSN-sync
+ * tickle when the TID is still module-blocked, leaving every downlink data
+ * frame queued in TQM forever (see the patch log). A WMI per-peer TID flush
+ * kicks the queues back to life; re-check once afterwards.
+ */
+#define ATH12K_TXBURST_CHECK_DELAY_MS	1500
+#define ATH12K_TXBURST_MIN_ATTEMPTS	4
+
+static void ath12k_mac_sta_txburst_check_wk(struct wiphy *wiphy,
+					    struct wiphy_work *work)
+{
+	struct ath12k_sta *ahsta = container_of(work, struct ath12k_sta,
+						txburst_check_wk.work);
+	struct ieee80211_sta *sta = ath12k_ahsta_to_sta(ahsta);
+	struct ath12k_vif *ahvif = ahsta->ahvif;
+	struct ath12k_hw *ah;
+	u32 attempts, acked;
+
+	lockdep_assert_wiphy(wiphy);
+
+	if (!ahvif)
+		return;
+
+	ah = ahvif->ah;
+
+	if (!ahsta->txburst_check_armed ||
+	    ahsta->state != IEEE80211_STA_AUTHORIZED)
+		return;
+
+	attempts = atomic_read(&ahsta->txburst_attempts);
+	acked = atomic_read(&ahsta->txburst_acked);
+
+	if (acked || attempts < ATH12K_TXBURST_MIN_ATTEMPTS) {
+		/* Healthy, or not enough traffic to judge: stand down. */
+		WRITE_ONCE(ahsta->txburst_check_armed, false);
+		return;
+	}
+
+	if (!ahsta->txburst_flushed) {
+		ath12k_hw_warn(ah,
+			       "peer %pM: first TX burst dead (a=%u ok=%u), flushing TIDs (first-assoc lost-wakeup workaround)\n",
+			       sta->addr, attempts, acked);
+		ath12k_mac_op_flush_sta(ah->hw, ath12k_ahvif_to_vif(ahvif), sta);
+		ahsta->txburst_flushed = true;
+		atomic_set(&ahsta->txburst_attempts, 0);
+		atomic_set(&ahsta->txburst_acked, 0);
+		wiphy_delayed_work_queue(wiphy, &ahsta->txburst_check_wk,
+					 msecs_to_jiffies(ATH12K_TXBURST_CHECK_DELAY_MS));
+		return;
+	}
+
+	ath12k_hw_warn(ah, "flush did not recover peer %pM (a=%u ok=%u)\n",
+		       sta->addr, attempts, acked);
+	WRITE_ONCE(ahsta->txburst_check_armed, false);
+}
+
 int ath12k_mac_op_sta_state(struct ieee80211_hw *hw,
 			    struct ieee80211_vif *vif,
 			    struct ieee80211_sta *sta,
@@ -7886,13 +7946,15 @@ int ath12k_mac_op_sta_state(struct ieee80211_hw *hw,
 	    new_state == IEEE80211_STA_NONE) {
 		memset(ahsta, 0, sizeof(*ahsta));
 		ahsta->free_logical_link_idx_map = U16_MAX;
+		wiphy_delayed_work_init(&ahsta->txburst_check_wk,
+					ath12k_mac_sta_txburst_check_wk);
 
 		arsta = &ahsta->deflink;
 
 		/* ML sta */
 		if (sta->mlo && !ahsta->links_map &&
 		    (hweight16(sta->valid_links) == 1)) {
-			ahsta->ml_peer_id = ath12k_peer_ml_alloc(ah);
+			ahsta->ml_peer_id = ath12k_peer_ml_alloc(ah, sta->addr);
 			if (ahsta->ml_peer_id == ATH12K_MLO_PEER_ID_INVALID) {
 				ath12k_hw_warn(ah, "unable to allocate ML peer id for sta %pM",
 					       sta->addr);
@@ -7974,6 +8036,17 @@ int ath12k_mac_op_sta_state(struct ieee80211_hw *hw,
 		ieee80211_set_active_links(vif, selected_links);
 	}
 
+	/* Station is going away or dropping out of AUTHORIZED: disarm the
+	 * first-TX-burst check so it cannot run against a dead station.
+	 */
+	if ((old_state == IEEE80211_STA_AUTHORIZED &&
+	     new_state == IEEE80211_STA_ASSOC) ||
+	    (old_state == IEEE80211_STA_NONE &&
+	     new_state == IEEE80211_STA_NOTEXIST)) {
+		WRITE_ONCE(ahsta->txburst_check_armed, false);
+		wiphy_delayed_work_cancel(hw->wiphy, &ahsta->txburst_check_wk);
+	}
+
 	/* Handle all the other state transitions in generic way */
 	valid_links = ahsta->links_map;
 	for_each_set_bit(link_id, &valid_links, IEEE80211_MLD_MAX_NUM_LINKS) {
@@ -8001,6 +8074,21 @@ int ath12k_mac_op_sta_state(struct ieee80211_hw *hw,
 		}
 	}
 
+	/* AP mode (including AP MLD): downlink data starts flowing once the
+	 * station is authorized. Arm a one-shot check for the dead first TX
+	 * burst signature.
+	 */
+	if (vif->type == NL80211_IFTYPE_AP &&
+	    old_state == IEEE80211_STA_ASSOC &&
+	    new_state == IEEE80211_STA_AUTHORIZED) {
+		atomic_set(&ahsta->txburst_attempts, 0);
+		atomic_set(&ahsta->txburst_acked, 0);
+		ahsta->txburst_flushed = false;
+		WRITE_ONCE(ahsta->txburst_check_armed, true);
+		wiphy_delayed_work_queue(hw->wiphy, &ahsta->txburst_check_wk,
+					 msecs_to_jiffies(ATH12K_TXBURST_CHECK_DELAY_MS));
+	}
+
 	if (ieee80211_vif_is_mld(vif) && vif->type == NL80211_IFTYPE_STATION &&
 	    old_state == IEEE80211_STA_ASSOC && new_state == IEEE80211_STA_AUTHORIZED) {
 		for_each_ar(ah, ar, i) {
@@ -8039,6 +8127,9 @@ peer_delete:
 	ath12k_dp_peer_delete(&ah->dp_hw, sta->addr, sta);
 ml_peer_id_clear:
 	if (sta->mlo) {
+		ath12k_info(ath12k_ah_to_ar(ah, 0)->ab,
+			    "ml peer id %u freed for %pM\n",
+			    ahsta->ml_peer_id, sta->addr);
 		if (!test_bit(ahsta->ml_peer_id, ah->quarantined_ml_peer_id_map))
 			clear_bit(ahsta->ml_peer_id, ah->free_ml_peer_id_map);
 		ahsta->ml_peer_id = ATH12K_MLO_PEER_ID_INVALID;
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/peer.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/peer.c
index 2e69437..dc40224 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/peer.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/peer.c
@@ -363,9 +363,10 @@ int ath12k_peer_create(struct ath12k *ar, struct ath12k_link_vif *arvif,
 	return ret;
 }
 
-u16 ath12k_peer_ml_alloc(struct ath12k_hw *ah)
+u16 ath12k_peer_ml_alloc(struct ath12k_hw *ah, const u8 *addr)
 {
 	u16 ml_peer_id = ah->last_ml_peer_id;
+	u16 cursor = ah->last_ml_peer_id;
 	int i;
 
 	lockdep_assert_wiphy(ah->hw->wiphy);
@@ -383,6 +384,9 @@ u16 ath12k_peer_ml_alloc(struct ath12k_hw *ah)
 
 		set_bit(ml_peer_id, ah->free_ml_peer_id_map);
 		ah->last_ml_peer_id = ml_peer_id;
+		ath12k_info(ath12k_ah_to_ar(ah, 0)->ab,
+			    "ml peer id %u allocated (cursor %u) for %pM\n",
+			    ml_peer_id, cursor, addr);
 		return ml_peer_id;
 	}
 
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/peer.h b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/peer.h
index 3c4f8bd..7ce6890 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/peer.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/peer.h
@@ -36,7 +36,7 @@ void ath12k_link_sta_rhash_delete(struct ath12k_base *ab, struct ath12k_link_sta
 int ath12k_link_sta_rhash_add(struct ath12k_base *ab, struct ath12k_link_sta *arsta);
 struct ath12k_link_sta *ath12k_link_sta_find_by_addr(struct ath12k_base *ab,
 						     const u8 *addr);
-u16 ath12k_peer_ml_alloc(struct ath12k_hw *ah);
+u16 ath12k_peer_ml_alloc(struct ath12k_hw *ah, const u8 *addr);
 void ath12k_peer_ml_quarantine(struct ath12k_hw *ah,
 			       struct ath12k_sta *ahsta, int reason);
 #endif /* _PEER_H_ */
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/dp_tx.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/dp_tx.c
index 632230e..e4d6002 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/dp_tx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/dp_tx.c
@@ -857,6 +857,14 @@ static void ath12k_wifi7_dp_tx_complete_msdu(struct ath12k_pdev_dp *dp_pdev,
 		goto exit;
 	}
 
+	/* Feed the first-TX-burst self-heal check. */
+	if (ts->status == HAL_WBM_TQM_REL_REASON_FRAME_ACKED) {
+		struct ath12k_sta *ahsta = ath12k_sta_to_ahsta(peer->sta);
+
+		if (unlikely(READ_ONCE(ahsta->txburst_check_armed)))
+			atomic_inc(&ahsta->txburst_acked);
+	}
+
 	status.sta = peer->sta;
 	status.info = info;
 	status.skb = msdu;
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/hw.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/hw.c
index 97b3987..1659e8f 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/hw.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/hw.c
@@ -996,6 +996,13 @@ static void ath12k_wifi7_mac_op_tx(struct ieee80211_hw *hw,
 		ahsta = ath12k_sta_to_ahsta(control->sta);
 		if (ahsta && ahsta->enable_4addr)
 			arsta = rcu_dereference(ahsta->link[link_id]);
+
+		/* Feed the first-TX-burst self-heal check: count unicast
+		 * data enqueues while the post-authorize probe is armed.
+		 */
+		if (ahsta && !is_mcast &&
+		    unlikely(READ_ONCE(ahsta->txburst_check_armed)))
+			atomic_inc(&ahsta->txburst_attempts);
 	}
 
 	/* This is case only for P2P_GO */
